diff --git a/docs/internationalization.md b/docs/internationalization.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3bd3da4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/internationalization.md
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# Languages
+
+Fizzy supports English (`en`, the default) and Japanese (`ja`). Open any application
+page with `?locale=ja` to switch; use `?locale=en` to switch back. Other values are
+ignored. No browser language detection changes the default English experience.
+
+Run `bin/rails db:migrate` when deploying: the preference is stored on `Identity`,
+not on an account membership. Anonymous choices live in the Rails session and are
+saved to the identity after successful authentication. An authenticated choice is
+saved immediately. A fresh browser recovers the preference on sign-in.
+
+## Rendering
+
+- `CurrentLocale` scopes requests with `I18n.with_locale`, including early redirects.
+- Mailers select the recipient's language when rendering, including queued mail.
+  Magic links also accept an explicit pre-authentication choice without changing
+  the recipient's saved preference.
+- User-specific notification and pin broadcasts capture the recipient's locale.
+- Locale is included in fragment cache keys and ETags. Public views use private
+  HTTP caching because their language can depend on a session cookie.
+- A locale change reloads Turbo's persistent UI and clears old-language offline pages. Application JavaScript reads its
+  translations from the current page; dates use the document language rather than
+  the browser's language. English relative-date wording is retained.
+- Static error pages are bilingual and do not need a session or Rails rendering.
+
+Application text is in `config/locales/en.yml` and `ja.yml`; Rails' Japanese date,
+number, validation and attribute labels are in `ja.rails.yml`. Use interpolation
+for dynamic values. Keep technical identifiers (routes, enum values, CSS classes,
+API keys) stable. Resolve label maps at use time, not at class load time. User names,
+board names and authored rich text are content, not translation keys. The rich-text
+editor's own JavaScript package is intentionally unchanged.
+
+## Verification
+
+```sh
+bin/rails test test/controllers/locales_test.rb \
+  test/integration/internationalization_test.rb \
+  test/mailers/localized_mailers_test.rb \
+  test/models/translations_test.rb test/models/localized_updates_test.rb
+```
+
+The tests cover persistence, invalid parameters, request isolation, public pages,
+Japanese screen-reader labels, queued and operational mail, dates, counts, live
+updates, historical system comments, onboarding, catalog parity, and error pages.
+Run the existing suite as well to check English compatibility.
